  {
    title: "How would you design a hotel reservation system?",
    answer:
      "## Design Hotel Reservation System\n\nMust prevent **double-booking** under concurrency.\n\n| Step | Pattern |\n|---|---|\n| Availability | `rooms` table + `inventory` per `date` row, `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` or `optimistic version` |\n| Hold | `Redis` lock `SET NX EX 10m` on `hotel+date` → create `PENDING` reservation |\n| Payment | `Saga` `reserve → pay → confirm` + `outbox` for idempotency |\n| Search | `Elasticsearch` + `geohash` + `date` filter |\n\n**Interview tip:** mention `idempotency key` on reserve.",
    examples: [
      {
        label: "Reserve with lock",
        variants: [
          { tech: "python", runnable: true, code: "import time\nlocks={}\ndef reserve(hotel,date):\n    key=f\"{hotel}:{date}\"\n    if locks.get(key): return False\n    locks[key]=time.time()+600\n    print('hold',key)\n    return True\nprint(reserve('h1','2025-08-31'))\nprint(reserve('h1','2025-08-31'))" },
          { tech: "javascript", runnable: true, code: "const locks=new Map();\nfunction reserve(h,d){\n  const k=`${h}:${d}`;\n  if(locks.has(k)) return false;\n  locks.set(k,Date.now()+600000);\n  console.log('hold',k); return true;\n}\nconsole.log(reserve('h1','2025-08-31'));\nconsole.log(reserve('h1','2025-08-31'));" },
          { tech: "go", runnable: false, code: "package main\nimport \"fmt\"\nvar locks=map[string]bool{}\nfunc reserve(h,d string) bool{ k:=h+\":\"+d; if locks[k]{return false}; locks[k]=true; fmt.Println(\"hold\",k); return true}\nfunc main(){ fmt.Println(reserve(\"h1\",\"2025-08-31\"))}" },
          { tech: "java", runnable: false, code: "import java.util.*;\npublic class Main{ static Set<String> locks=new HashSet<>(); static boolean reserve(String h,String d){String k=h+\":\"+d; if(!locks.add(k)) return false; System.out.println(\"hold \"+k); return true;} public static void main(String[] a){System.out.println(reserve(\"h1\",\"2025-08-31\"));}}" },
        ],
      },
